-- CK-120: explicit `Basics.eq` on a `type` that wraps a schema endpoint
-- whose `via` target holds a function is `not_equatable` (checker-v2.md
-- §11.4 *as amended by R8b's review round*), in its own module and in an
-- importer. The structural gate of a `type` is "no function reachable from
-- its payloads", through its module's endpoints and their `via` targets —
-- the same fact `==` reads off the derived contexts — and an importer reads
-- it from the record. On 7427828, and in v2 before R8b's review round, the
-- gate was the table-build bit ("no function in its declaration"), which
-- cannot see a `via` target: `==` on `Holds` was refused and `Basics.eq`
-- on it accepted, two answers to one question.
import B


viaEq : Bool
viaEq =
    B.mk 1 == B.mk 2


viaBasics : Bool
viaBasics =
    Basics.eq (B.mk 1) (B.mk 2)
